Summary: why sendspace limited according to ethernet packet size
Keywords: socket, protocols, dli
X-Newsreader: NN version 6.5.0 (NOV)

the sendspace for dli which is intern setting the hiwater
mark for socket is limited to 2k in Ultrix and 5000 bytes
in case of ALPHA (OSF-1). 

I think that this makes dli interface exteremly
inefficient because tcp  allows upto 64k hiwater mark. so
We have to read one packet at a time (packet size limited
by these factors ) which in itself is quite time
consuming. If we fragment the packet after the socket call
somewhere inside dli_usrreq.c etc, it should be more
efficient or make inside the socket layer code
uipc_socket.c. 

I would like some feedback from the developers of this dli
interface in DEC.

