From the back of the manual "VCB02 video Subsystem Technical
Manual" (AZ-GLGAB-MN)...


		Mouse Cable Connector
		      End View

			 +
		       5 6 7
		      3     4
		      +1   2+

	+ Connector Key

Pin Number		Function
 1			GND (signal and power return)
 2			TXD (serial out from mouse)
 3			RXD (serial in to mounse)
 4			-12V
 5			+5V
 6			Not Used
 7			Device Present (shorted to pin 1)
 Shell			Protective ground

The mouse runs at 4800 baud, 8-bits, odd parity.  Mouse reports
are 3 bytes:

	1  0  0 sx sy  L  M  R
	0 x6 x5 x4 x3 x2 x1 x0
	0 y6 y5 y4 y3 y2 y1 y0

	Bit 7 - Frame synch
	SX SY - Sign bit 1 = positive, 0 = negative
	LMR   - Button state 1 = depressed
	X6-0  - X displacement
	Y6-0  - Y displacement

Power up sequence is 4 bytes, first byte has bits 7 and 5 set to
indicate this is the power up sequence.  I won't go into the details
of the report.  Only the second byte is interesting.  If the upper
nibble = 0010 it is the mouse, if it is 0100 it is the serial tablet.

Commands:

	R	- select stream mode
	D	- Prompt mode
	P	- Request mouse report
	T	- Self test

Note that the mouse is half-duplex, and will not accept commands
while it is sending data.  This is mostly of concern after getting
the power-up sequence.  You must wait at least 500ms after a power
up command completes before sending it commands.  Other commands
require 50ms.  Power up is within 1sec of stable power.


