>Sorry, no.  You must use a postscripter or interpeter. The
>LN03a was optimized for printing images.

The LN03A (low-memory ANSI laser printer) and the LN03Q (image printer) are
being confused here. But the rest of the reply is basically correct. DECwrite
produces PostScript output. I'd suggest PSprint to print it to an ANSI laser
but the LN03A doesn't have a full bitmap like the LN03S (LN03PLUS) and you
might end up with a page complexity problem.
