I ran across in interesting variation on this, not involving PTY's.  Once
logged in, the monitor (of course) would *NOT* allow you to execute

	.LOGIN proj,prog

However one could run SYS:LOGIN while logged in by simply doing:

	.R LOGIN

And before LOGIN would error out (complaing that you were already logged-in)
it would first clear your <(I think the term was search list)>, thus allowing
you to LOGOUT since you had no disks on which to check a loggged-out quota.

Unfortunately, for me (I was a - very inquisitive - student at the time), I
shared this info. w/ one too many other students, so eventually our systems'
programmer found out about it and patched LOGIN; and I had to explore other
ways of keeping a lot of <junk> online, like the already-mentioned [3,3]
queue-spooling areas.

