I've been poking around with two 5.25" floppy drives, in an attempt
to get either one up & running as an RX33.  Last I heard, an RX33
was actually a TEAC FD55-GFR.

I have *TWO* FD55's in front of me, and they are ELECTRONICALLY different.

One is an FD-55GFR-570-U (an older drive,) and the other
    is an FD-55GFR-149-U5.

Both drives have several jumpers available, but I'd imagine that
neither is set up like DEC's RX33.  Also note that the older drive
does NOT have a terminator installed, although there is a 16-pin
dip socket for one, and the newer drive has in-line network soldered
on the board.


I've reached a few conclusions, although some of them may be in error:

The floppy cable appears to be a straight-thru type, rather than the
usual twisted cable found on PC's.  I figured this was going to be the
case. 

The drive needs to be set to Drive Select 2 (0-3), just like the
hard drives.  Configurations using DS0 and DS1 return non-existent
drive messages.


I'm using (obviously) an RQDX3, installed in a BA23 chassis,
and a 4-button panel.  The controller is known to be good.


The best I've managed so far is one of two errors -

Drive error, or Disk not loaded (no media present)

(Although I had a bootable RX50 in the drive)


If anyone has a more specific model number, I'd like to
know what it is.  Better yet, if anyone has jumper settings
for either of these drives, let me know!

Each drive appears to have a different set of jumpers available:

The older style FD-55GFR-570-U has:

U0, U1, D0-D3, LG, and EZ located between the power connector & terminator.
Directly behind the power connector, near the board edge is FG, 
and near the center of the board is I, II, and IS.  
Behind the terminator is IU, ML, RY, and DC2.

The newer style FD-55GFR-149-U5 has:

U0, U1, D0-D3 between the power connector & terminator.
Directly behind the power connector, near the board-edge, is FG,
and there is an unmarked jumper about 1/2 inch away from that, towards
the center of the board.
Directly behind the terminator is a whole slew of jumpers -
LG, IS, DC, RY, IU, ML, and I.


Any help would be appreciated.

(I do NOT have access to FTP)



