"Ian" == Ian Staples <ianst@qdpii.ind.dpi.qld.gov.au> writes:

>    Ian> A most useful feature which wasn't disabled in 5 was the ability
>    Ian> to write to other directories.  With a bit of preparation you
>    Ian> could copy large files to another area and so avoid the logout
>    Ian> limits on disk space :):):)

Back when I was a student at WPI, one of the major activities was to
find out how to log out over quota.  Back then each student was given
a base of 100 blocks and had to formally request more and be able to
justify it.

At the time, the machine was a KA-10 running the TOPS-10 5.07 monitor
and WPI was a beta test site.

Well, I was debugging a program one day which used a WPI-defined
UUO, WPILGO (logout).  The program didn't seem to be logging out
so I figured I had done it improperly.  I fired up IDDT to debug
it and when I got to that UUO, it worked!

Turns out I was over quota at the time, so as a single job, I
couldn't log out unless I removed some files.  But when I ran the
IDDT job, the log out succeeded because there were multiple jobs
with the same PPN.  The other job (the IDDT one) would be killed
by DAEMON, after it determined that IDDT didn't have a controlling
terminal.  Voila', logged out over quota...

Well, I wasn't looking for a method (really I wasn't... I had already
gotten an extension...)  so I reported it to the system manager
who was also quite good at TOPS-10 monitor internals and he had it
fixed inside an hour...

					Megan Gentry
					Former WPI hacker
					Former RT-11 Developer



