The audio device driver is shipped with DEC OSF/1, but I'm not sure whether
it's built into the default kernel.  In any case, the cctual name of the
device when it is available is /dev/streams/bba.

To use the device you need to install Multimedia Services for OSF/1 which
has the server that manages the device and the support libraries along
with some starter applets.  If your system was delivered recently and
has Factory Installed Software, this product should already be preinstalled
for you.  Otherwise, you'll need to install it from the Layered Products CD.

The license for Multimedia Services is bundled with all the Alpha
workstations that run DEC OSF/1.

