writes:
>What's the difference?
>
The RZ26B is an HP drive buyout qualified for use in certain systems.
The RZ26-E is an RZ26 (like DSP3105) with an option.
An RZ26E-something would surprise me.
An RZ26-B would be an RZ26 with a certain option. There could even be an
RZ26B-B
or an RZ26B-E.
The RZ26L-something is a DSP3107L but with DEC firmware and just 1.05 GB, FWIW.

You have to pay close attention to the part number "syntax", i.e. if a letter
comes before or after the dash. Before the dash is the base part number,
after the dash is the option.

