>      inet 192.36.171.42 --> 192.36.171.61 netmask ffffffe0  ipmtu 296 
> 
> Have anyone usep SLIP on these machines, and how should I configure it
> to work properly.

It's not enough to define the interface IP.
You have to add a route und to enable forwarding using "iprsetup".

I got it to work with the follwing entries in gated.conf:

passiveinterfaces 141.61.1.40 141.61.80.2
net 141.61.80.0 gateway 141.61.80.2 metric 4 rip


141.61.1.40 is the ethernet interface,
the slip interface has 141.61.80.1, but as given in the gated man pages
one has the specify the other end of a point-to-point line as 
passive (alawys up).
The second line adds a permanent route for the slip line. Without this
entry the 141.61.80.0 subnet wasn't announced on the local ethernet via
RIP.

Herbert Hanewinkel


