In article <westman.776976533@cynthia>, westman@tp.umu.se (Olof Westman)
writes:
>We have tried to use HP DATs 35480A 
>and C1533A on DEC 3000/300X and LX
>running OSF1. The DATs are SCSI
>devices and work just perfectly except
>for one thing: the bootup test. The
>boot program stops and reports the
>following error:
>?? 002 SCSI  0x0008
>
>Failed 84
>

This is a complete WAG, but at the console, type:

show scsi_reset

It will probably be some small integer.  If it is less than 4, try increasing
it some.  (You may have to increase it by powers of 2 -- I forget). 

Tapes and CD-ROM drives are notoriously slow to answer resets and
the console may not be waiting long enough for the device to answer before
deciding the thing has timed out and died.

Note.  Upping this number increases system boot time by a human-perceptible
amount.
