I use a tz87 on a DECstation 5000/240 with DECnsr (legato networker). I
like it a lot. Its been much faster than the DAT drive, its never broke in
the 6 or so months that ive had it. My nsr log looks like its backing up
around 10MB/minute, but nsr interleaves writes, so im not sure if that
number means much. Ive got another one that I could try with dump, email
if youre interested. 

As far as the future of DLT, I think its pretty good. I think the format
is technically superior to 8mm or DAT, and even before Digital sold the
storage stuff, they had started to sell it outside the DEC base. I think
Dell announced they were puting them on their PC servers for example.

