> I am looking for a better mousetrap for backups ( currently using 4mm)
> and would like to know if anyone is using DLT.  I would be using them
> on SUN hardware.  If you are using them what is your data throughput (real  >world)  how reliable.  Any comments on its future?
>

	Well, we use them.  :-) Not surprising since we are the developers.

	The real world throughput is determined mostly by factors other
	than the tape drive, namely:

		- host platform 
		- host adapter
		- host bus configuration
		- host software
		- record size
		- compression characteristics

	The DLT's have caches which are large enough to compensate for
	bursty host transmission, and if the real world throughput is
	less than the DLTs capability, it is likely caused by some
	other bottleneck (see above).

	Which DLT are you considering ?

	As far as the future goes, I can say that future generations are
	planned and presently under development.  Of course, our new
	owners (Quantum, as of 3-Oct-1994) will likely have a lot to
	say about our future strategy.  So far, they've indicated that
	they are commited to continue to invest in the DLT technology.
	

