        I haven't figured out the  general  solution to finding out what
    resources  an  application  uses.  I'd sure like to know  _all_  the
    applicable  resources  for  EVE  and  TPU.   For  window  size   and
    placement,  and titles, you can copy SYS$LIBRARY:TPU.DAT and EVE.DAT
    to your DECW$USER_DEFAULTS, and modify them to suit you.

        Here are a couple extracts from past posts to vmsnet.tpu on
    selecting the small versus large fonts (or condensed versus normal):

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<From: walsh@sparty.zko.dec.com (Chris Walsh)>
[...]
Or you can do what I do, and modify some X default values that TPU uses.  
    (Actually, the DECterm widget that TPU is built upon.)  I include my own 
    defaults - your tastes may vary:

    #
    # Have TPU startup using the condensed, little font
    #
    Tpu*condensedFont:      on
    Tpu*fontSetSelection:   1
    #
    # Use 48 lines and 80 columns.
    #
    Tpu.Tpu$MainWindow.X:           0
    Tpu.Tpu$MainWindow.Y:           145
    Tpu.Tpu$MainWindow.Columns:     80
    Tpu.Tpu$MainWindow.Rows:        48
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<From: m_reymond@zeus.dev.macsch.com (Mike Reymond)>
[...]

Copy the resource file: SYS$LIBRARY:TPU.DAT into your default login directory
and add the following lines:

Tpu*FontSetSelection:		0
#Tpu*condensedFont:		on

The first line gives you the same font as the Big Font on a DecTerm. But at 132
columns, as you say, it all doesn't fit on the screen. Uncomment the second
line for 132 columns.  
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
From: "robinson@tle.enet.dec.com  05-Mar-1992 0845" <robinson@tle.enet.dec.com>

! The parameters correspond to the following X resources that you can put
! into your TPU or EVE resource files.  On VMS copy TPU.DAT or EVE.DAT
! from SYS$LIBRARY and define the logical name TPU$DEFAULTS to point to
! your modified file.  On ULTRIX, copy tpu or eve from
! /usr/lib/X11/app-defaults to your directory, and specify the -X option
! followed by your filespec.
!
! For tiny fonts:
!     Tpu*condensedFont:		on
!     Tpu*fontSetSelection:		1
! For huge fonts:
!     Tpu*condensedFont:		off
!     Tpu*fontSetSelection:       	0
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------


        All of this  implies  to  me  that  you  can  choose between the
    _DECTerm_  big  or small font via Tpu*fontSetSelection, and  between
    the wide and narrow font via Tpu*condensedFont.  So if you know  how
    to  change  the  DECterm fonts, the TPU window might follow.  I just
    wish the documentation (or somebody) would come out and LIST all the
    resources that an application uses.  :-(

        -Ken
