    Another reason for slowness.

    DLTs work best with large record sizes.  While not that much of a
    factor on TZ85/THZ01 or TZ86/THZ02, it can be a dramatic factor on
    TZ87/DLT2000.  To get optimal tape drive capability, at least 8KB
    records must be used.  If you can use larger records, do so.  Ideally,
    32K or 64K are recommended.

    Some host application programs (particularly on PCs and UNIX boxes)
    use 512 byte records.  This will tend to reduce a DLT2000's
    performance down to a couple hundred KB/sec.


