>>     I don't think that's quite right.  Here's a somewhat more correct
>>version (mainly right ...)
> 
> Still not entirely correct, but better... :-)
> 
>>PDP-1 begets PDP-4 begets PDP-7 begets PDP-9 begets PDP-15, 18 bits
>>PDP-5 begets PDP-8, PDP-8 + Linc = Linc-8 begets PDP-12, 12 bits
>>PDP-6 begets PDP-10 begets PDP-20, 36 bits
> 
> The most common mistake. There never was any such beast as the
> pdp-20. It's just the plain pdp-10 even when DEC called it DECsystem-20.

Correct.  There are two differences between a DECsystem10 and a DECSYSTEM20:

1.	Microcode
2.	Capitalization

(10s were painted blue, and 20s orange, but the microcode made the real
difference.  Last time I went for TOPS training at Bedford, the blue machine
was running TOPS-20 that week and the orange one TOPS-10.  We replaced a 1090
system with two 2060s, and one of them ran TOPS-10 for a semester until we got
the users migrated.  DECSYSTEM20 microcode had different paging, and some
interesting additions to the byte pointer implementation.)
