  Yes, the 11/73 is a J-11 based system, as was the 11/53, 11/83,
11/84, 11/93, and 11/94.

  The Fuji M2311...I've never even _seen_ one of those.  The M2312K is
8" SMD, 67mb formatted, 84mb unformatted, same geometries as the good
ole' RM02/03.  In fact, the most common way for a DEC system to access
a M2312K is to emulate an RM02, or sometimes several logical RK07's.

  The Fuji Eagle is a different animal altogether.  Its model number
is M2351, it's 10.5" high, 19" wide (rackmounted), and weighs about
140lbs.  It's 474mb unformatted with an average access time of around
18ms.  Also VERY reliable.  The interface is SMD, and to my knowledge,
no dual-port option was available until the introduction of the Super
Eagle (M2361, ~630mb).

  Good luck with your 11/73; I love those boxes.  If you want to part
with it, drop me a line.  Maybe we could swap stuff or I'd even be
willing to buy it from you if you're interested.


