You might want to make sure that the kernel has been configured for a
disk at SCSI id 4.  Look for a line that looks like this:

device disk     rz4        at asc0      drive     32

in your kernel config file (/sys/conf/NAME).  If it's not there, add it,
rebuild the kernel, install the new kernel and reboot. 

