Online documentation tends to be in a separate subset.
In this case, the man pages for slattach and sliphosts
are to be found in UDXMAN.

>I need to get SLIP running on my DECStation - It installed a couple
>of .o files and a program called slattach, and not much else...

>How can I set SLIP up?!

You'll need to add "pseudodevice sl" to your configuration
file and build a new kernel, then edit "/etc/sliphosts" to
define the host(s) you'll connect to (comments in the file are
equivalent to the man page). 
Connect using "slattach host" where host is the name defined
in sliphosts, and slattach will do the dialing (if necessary)
and the ifconfig.  Add a route for the connection and you're all
set.

I just did it on Friday, and I can testify it works pretty well.
