In Article <garner-1708941403370001@141.224.128.240>
garner@aug3.augsburg.edu (Joseph C. Garner) writes:
>I need to get some postscript files from a VAX to an AppleTalk printer. 
>Is there a way to save the files in a standard postscript format?

I think you need to be clearer. If the file is PostScript, it is PostScript.
Just FTP it or whatever. PostScript files on a VAX are identical to PostScript
files anywhere else. Just remember that they are ASCII files and binary
transfer will really screw them up!

If you can plug the AppleTalk printer into the VAX directly, you can just copy
the file to the port the printer is plugged into. You can do similar things
with a terminal server port.

If you want to print to an AppleTalk printer on the network, you will need an
AppleTalk package such as Pathworks for VMS (Macintosh).

If yoou are looking for something else, you'll have to explain what it is
better, I'm afraid.

