In article <32mjj8$1no@usenet.INS.CWRU.Edu>, ce676@cleveland.Freenet.Edu
(Edward E. Madden) writes:

|>I am upgrading my MicroVAX II to an Alpha 3000/600s.  Do I have
|>to create a new UAF file or can I copy my old one from the
|>MicroVAX?  I have about 400 users and I don't want to enter
|>all the UAF records by hand.  Is there a utility that can do
|>it for me?  I have gone through the documentation and they
|>don't mention upgrading from a VAX to Alpha.  I am running 
|>version 5.5 on the VAX. What about the rights database and ACL's
|>and stuff like that?

  I do not believe there were any changes to the format of the
  SYSUAF among OpenVMS VAX V5.5, OpenVMS AXP V1.5, OpenVMS VAX
  V6.1 and OpenVMS AXP V6.1.  V6.1 did introduce a new proxy
  database file format, but the old database is (currently)
  maintained in parallel.

  The rightslist and sysuaf formats are compatible across OpenVMS
  versions that can coexist in a VMScluster.  And assuming that the
  AXP rightslist has not been tailored, you should have no problems
  with ACL conflicts.  (Sharing the authorization database -- which
  is similar to what you want to do -- is covered in the _Guide to
  VMSclusters_.)

  Other files to consider: SYSUAF, SYSALF, VMSMAIL_PROFILE,
  RIGHTSLIST, QMAN$MASTER, NETPROXY, NETOBJECT, AUDIT_SERVER,
  VMS$PASSWORD_HISTORY, UCX$CONFIGURATION, UCX$EXPORT, UCX$HOST,
  UCX$PROXY, UCX$ROUTE, UCX$SERVICE, SYLOGIN, SYS$ANNOUNCE,
  SYS$WELCOME

  If these were my boxes, I'd look at upgrading the MicroVAX II to
  OpenVMS VAX V6.1, and running the two systems in parallel until
  I was fully settled in over on the AXP.  (One can configure these
  systems into a VMScluster, though it's not necessary.) 

  This upgrade top OpenVMS V6.1 serves two purposes: Running the
  two systems in parallel means you have somewhere to fall back to
  until you have routed out all of the VAX images and are running
  native on the AXP. It also means that all versions of all system
  data files are compatible.

  --

  General rules: No more than two OpenVMS versions, or one version
  on each platform, is supported in the same VMScluster.  And the
  "migration" support is the rolling upgrade -- it is intended to
  get the VMScluster into the "warranted" configuration.

                     +-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+
                     | AXP V6.1  | VAX V6.1  | VAX V6.0  | AXP V1.5  |
       +-------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+
       | VAX V5.5-2  | Migration | Migration | Migration | WARRANTED |
       +-------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+-----------+
       | AXP V1.5    | Migration | Migration | WARRANTED |
       +-------------+-----------+-----------+-----------+
       | VAX V6.0    | Migration | Migration |
       +-------------+-----------+-----------+
       | VAX V6.1    | WARRANTED |
       +-------------+-----------+

  
