	There was a variant of the DS5000/25 which came set for use with
the VR297.  Do you know what monitor it used to have?  Also, if the on-board
HX is like the PMAGB-BA card, you need the proper crystal in the  second
socket.  The PMAGB-Bx came with a 72Hz crystal soldered in plus either a
60, 66, or 72 Hz crystal in the second socket.  If you don't have the right
crystal in the second socket, you need to replace it with the 60Hz crystal.
See if there is a file with *sfb* on gatekeeper somewhere, maybe under
pub/DEC/TriAdd.  I may have at least a paper copy of the table somewhere.
You may also need the proper (good) cable.

>Unfortunately, I don't remember where the jumpers or switches are, nor
>even how to tell for sure which board that you have, other than that
>the HX only requires a single TurboChannel slot (but so do most of the
>others).

