In article <13AUG199410052681@almach.caltech.edu> shoppa@almach.caltech.edu
(Timothy D. Shoppa x4256) writes:

>I strongly the believe the best route to take would be creation of a
>comp.sys.dec.pdp (or similarly-named) newsgroup, which would cover all older
>DEC hardware.

Except that this misses the very important point that these systems have little
in common besides the manufacturer:  Word sizes vary from 12 through 18 to 36,
with a side-jaunt to 16, and instruction sets go from very simple (PDP-8, for
example) to very large but regular (PDP-10).

This suggestion makes no more sense than suggesting that IBM 360s, 1400s,
70[49].?s, System/3, System/7, and so on  belong in one group because they are
all "Blue."

And I, for one, would vote against any comp.sys. placement for the PDP-10
group.  The alt.sys. heirarchy seems the right place for 36-bit needs.
