: It depends on what sort of TurboChannel video adaptor your 5000/25 has.

Actually, although 5000/25 has two TC slots, it has also a graphics
controller on the mo-bo, and most 5000/25 on the market, i Think, are using
this configuration. 

This controller is as-far-as-I-remember, 1024x768@72Hz,
and there is no switch to change it to something else. VR297 doesn't work
since this is 1024x860@60Hz, but your chances of find SVGA Multisinc PC
monitor that will be adequate are much better. Or try to locate VRC16.

If you insist on using the VR297 then, as said CX or one of HX types will
work (not all of them. I think that just PMAGB-BA). CX are much now obsolete
and you may find one for free (we have here some as junk, but I am too
far for you ...), but word of caution: CX on half-speed Turbochannel (as
DS5000/25 is) has a bug that gives it awfull scrolling performance. This
is the reason we changed them all to HX. The internal native controller
is much better.

Good Luck
