>We happen to have the weird combination of a Pers. DECstation 5000/25 and 
>an old VRD297-D4 monitor from a DECstation 2100 (remember those ?).  Anyhow 
>the 5000/25 doesn't seem to like the monitor.
>
>Is there any way to get the 5000/25 to talk to this older monitor ?  [...]

It depends on what sort of TurboChannel video adaptor your 5000/25 has.
The possibilities I remember are the MX, CX, PX, PXG (with several
variants), HX, and TX - there may be one or two others (ZX?).  The only
ones of those listed above which stand a chance of working with a VR297
are the CX and the HX.  Luckily, the HX was the most commonly used board,
so I'm betting that that's what you have.  Most HXs are configured by
default to use a 72 MHz monitor with different screen resolution than the
VR297, but all it takes to switch it is a jumper (or was it a dip switch?)
or two.

Unfortunately, I don't remember where the jumpers or switches are, nor
even how to tell for sure which board that you have, other than that
the HX only requires a single TurboChannel slot (but so do most of the
others).  There's one command in ULTRIX V4.2A and later that will give
you the video card in PMAG-whatever part number notation - the same
information is also available in the boot-time messages which you can
fetch via "/etc/uerf -R -r 300".  A listing of all of the possibilities
would make a really useful part of the comp.unix.ultrix FAQ.

Speaking of the FAQ - it's been quite a while since the ULTRIX and
DEC OSF/1 FAQs have been posted, haven't they?  (Actually, I think
I know why, but I'll refrain from saying so until I can get in touch
with the relevant person(s)...)

