In article <Cu0p20.2nA@ram.nl>, marc@ram.nl (Marc Gobes) writes:
> I'am working with Keaterm 2.2, an ms windows vt420 emulator
> but ran into an small problem. With my enhanced keyboard
> Keaterm maps every LK450 function key except the DO key.
> Does someone know the trick to map the DO key into an 
> normal pc keyboard, or the escape sequence for an DO key ?
> With the last one, I can generate my own mapping.

        The DO key is also know as  F16.   The HELP key is also known as
    F15.  In 7-bit escape sequences, these are

        	HELP = F15 = <esc>[28~
        	DO   = F16 = <esc>[29~

        I'm using KEAterm 340 V3.0.0.   It's  mainly  just a superset of
    KEAterm  420, but apparently a more recent version than yours.  I've
    had no trouble using the CONGIFURE - KEYBOARD - MAPPING menu to  set
    the Scroll Lock key to F15 and the Pause key to F16.

        -Ken
