An RRD40 is one of the first CD drives and uses a sony standard insert.

yes the insert is longer than a regular one, there is a plastic insert that
surrounds the disk... you slide the whole thing in and then pull the plastic
outer shell out... the cd and insert stay inside... it is a rad-only storage
device...

it normally is on a qbus system using a qbus controller module M7752-xx (also
referred to as the KRQ50 Option.

The other interface is a scsi interface....

it gets about 175 Kbytes/sec throughput, so about the speed of single speed
drives...

for reading... depends on the format of the CD...

I can mount pc &/or mac cds off the infoserver.  and vms cds on the vax
just like a regular disk... I think ultrix supports part of this but you may have
to check... I have the books on this drive, so if you need something specific,
just let me know... later...


