Those of us involved with the 10-Fami recall the different implementations
of the instructions set (and extensions) in two or more ways:
the processors were and are -10 processors (ka10, ki, ks, kl, kl10B, and KC!!)
They ran essetially the same instruction set.  Were packaged as various
systems - pdp10, dec10, dec 20.
The KL10 (or 2040 thru 65 or 1060 thru 90) with its limited capabilities
was faster  by a bit more than 10% than the vax 780.  The KS 10 (2020 processor)
was/is about the speed of an 11/70.  NOTE PLEASE that I said speed not
performance.  I am a 10/20 bigot who lived thru the purple plague
and still say that the vax and 11 families are 8 bit machines with
various size data busses.  the 10 is a true 36bit machine. And the bits
are numbered the proper way.

When XKL starts shipping (come on folks I want to see those puppies on
the net!!!!) One of the finest and most elegant architectures will be
alive again.

Bob



