In <Cu9x20.33G@adasoft.ch>, jw@adasoft.ch (Jamie Watson) writes:
)Does anyone know how to get the Ultrix "dd" to pad the last output block
)to whatever the specified block size is, when reading from stdin?  I know
)this sounds like a strange problem, and probably sounds more like user
)error than anything else, but I have been fighting with this for a very
)long time (several years, in fact), and I still can't get it to do what
)I want.  The kind of command line I am talking about is this:
)
)  compress < xc-1.tar | dd obs=10k conv=sync of=/dev/nrmt1l

	I would have thought this would work, but I guess there is a comflict
between obs= and conv=sync. If you made obs=2k or something, perhaps

   compress < xc-1.tar | dd obs=2k | dd bs=2k conv=sync of=/dev/nrmt1l

	would work.

	However, with the amount of time you have aprrently spent on this, you
could just write the half page C program to do the job.

