                       DECUS Australia 1994 Symposium

    The DECUS Australia 1994 Symposium will be held at the National
    Convention Centre, Canberra, from Saturday August 20th to Thursday
    August 25th, inclusive.

    Papers will be presented from Monday through to Thursday by Digital
    staff, Microsoft staff, other vendors, and of course end-users as well
    as invited experts including Keith Walls and Kevin Carosso.  There are
    over 200 papers in ten streams providing over 180 hours of information
    for all levels of expertise from notice to expert.  The Timetable is
    available from this WWW server in both ASCII text and PostScript
    formats, and a Speaker Listing is also available (ASCII text only).

    DECUS Educational Seminars will be held on Saturday and Sunday.  These
    full-day seminars are presented by speakers who are highly qualified to
    speak on their respective topics and range from experienced users to
    product developers.

    The annual Management Forum, aimed at covering business management
    issues in the I.T. sector, will be held on Sunday 21st August.  This
    year's theme is "Business Process Re-engineering -- What's That?" and
    is a must for senior managers.

    Full details are in the "DECUS Australia 1994 Symposium Registration
    Kit" available from the DECUS Office on (02) 561 5274, fax (02) 561
    5596.  Walk-in registrations are also welcome during the Symposium week.

    Further information is available on-line, via electronic mail and WWW:

    1.  The MAILSERV server at vsm.com.au can supply the following files:

    [SYMPOSIUM]MANAGEMENT.TXT		Management Forum timetable
    [SYMPOSIUM]SEMINAR_SUMMARY.TXT	Titles of each Seminar
    [SYMPOSIUM]SPEAKERS.TXT		List of Symposium Speakers
    [SYMPOSIUM]TIMETABLE.DOC		Symposium Timetable (DECwrite)
