Been there, done that - We had a MicroVAX 3600, ARC/INFO 5.0.2, we moved
to DEC 5000/25 desktop workstations, and a 5000/240 host /server.  Observations:
 
1. ESRI should tell you not to go the Ultrix route like we did in 1992, as
they will only be providing one release of ARC/Info 7.0 .  Given the bugginess
of their .0 releases, I dread loading it.  We are at 6.1.1, and although the
buglist is thicker than a pile of VMS 6.0 Release Notes, it is pretty stable
and consistent.  If I had it to do over, we'd have bought Sun, but at the time
DEC made all sorts of statements, innuendo, promises about the upgradeablilty
of the MIPS platform and most importantly in this context, the availability of
OSF/1 on MIPS.  ARC/Info will continue to evolve on OSF/1 running on AXP.
 
2. No matter which hardware platform you choose (Sun, HP, DG, even the newer
VAX4000) you'll be shoked at how fast that hummer screams!  The immediate
side effect is that you're staff wukk become so much more productive that
you will run out of disk space within 3 months of the upgrade!!  Be prepared
to invest heavily in both magnetic disk and more tape drives for backup.
 
3. Unix is not VMS.  Don't believe any vendor claims that their unix is
so innocuous that you'll never know that you made a change! Hah! No matter
how good the GUI, you do have to get your hands dirty in unix if you decide
to make the conversion.
4. Sun will definitely be the preferred platform for ARC/Info for the newxt
next several years.  This is no small item.
 
Good luck
 
