: decw$session on the remote pc, and then can start applications
: from the decw$session window.  We cannot start decw$terminal by
: from the VMS machine and have it display on the remote pc.


So I assume that you cannot start applications remotely from the PC.
If that's true then there's a good chance that 1) rexec is disabled or
malfunctioning on the VMS host.  2) PCX$SERVER.COM is not present or is
out of date.  3) If you are running Wollongong on the VMS host, you are not
using woll.com or are using an outdated one.    

If you can get more specific about what VMS TCP/IP you are using and 
any error messages you might be seeing, I'll see if I can come up with more
ideas.

Are you saying that you can start decw$session by pushing from the VMS side,
but not decterms?  Are you actually trying to run decw$terminal from a 
DCL prompt?  If so, use $CREATE/TERM/DET instead.  decw$terminal.exe 
is the decterm controller binary and shouldn't be executed directly.
eXcursion isn't really executing it either.  PCX$SERVER.COM converts any
references to decw$terminal over to $create/term/det for you.

: We have submitted the problem to DEC, but no solution yet.  I am
: wondering if others have seen this problem, and if anyone has 
: any ideas of how to solve it.

Remote start problems are probably the most common problem we see.
