I've just upgraded my old MicroVAX II by replacing the KA630 CPU and 9
megabytes of memory with a KA650 CPU and 16 megabytes of RAM.  At the
same time, I've added some more Qbus hardware, most importantly the
VCB02 graphics option.  Works great -- I'm running X11R6 with the R5
server, since support for the VCB0[12] (or Q[VD]SS) hardware was dropped
from R6.  However, Ultrix is causing me a spot of trouble:

I used to run Ultrix-32 4.3 on the KA630 with no problems.  Upgrading to
the KA650 processor (and performing a new, complete installation of
Ultrix, just to be absolutely certain everything was OK) caused the
clock to stop working.  All of a sudden, Ultrix was getting bogus time
from the hardware.  I suspected the NiCd battery had coincidentally gone
bad on me, but it seems to be OK.  I then upgraded to Ultrix-32 4.4, but
the clock still won't work right, and in addition to that, automatic
reboots of the system don't work either!  Doing "shutdown -r now" causes
the monitor to give a "DEVASSIGN" error, since it seems to be trying to
boot from a device called "_" instead of "DUA0" as it should.

However, shutting down and then rebooting manually makes the system come
up with the right time -- it's only when I turn the box off that it gets
it wrong.  The clock isn't zeroed, either; for instance I had the
machine turned off last night for about a minute or two, and it came up
with the date set to sometime on June 5th -- 56 days in the past.

Any ideas at all?  Grateful for any help!

-tih


