>    Owner process ID        00000000    Dev Prot   S:RWED,O:RWED,G:RWED,W:RWED
>    Reference count                0    Default buffer size             2048
>    Density                     6666    Format                     Normal-11
>
>  Volume status:  no-unload on dismount, beginning-of-tape, odd parity.


When all three lights are flashing it usually means the tape drive is in
never-never land. A complete power off usually clears it, if not then the
tape leader( this little black tape may have come loose. If you pull the 
TZ30 out a little take the cover off the system, there will be a little 
black latch next to a soleniod on the right side just behind the front 
cover of the tape drive. If the tape is not spinning hit the unload button
wait for the lights again and pull the latch back the tape should come out.
If there is some tape still stuck wound around the inside you might s.o.l.
When the tape comes out check the leader and rerun through the reels and
heads and hook it back up then see if it resets itself.
Finally if this system is under contract or warranty its a hell of a lot 
easier to call your local field service person, being a former DEC one 
myself calls like this were easy ones that were semi-enjoyable. If you
have neither and the instructions don't work call me and I'll try and help.
It's definetly a hardware problem and a complete power off will clear a
lot of those up.

Good Luck,


