We have seen this effect; in our case it meant that the leader tape which
is used to pull the tape out from the cartridge had fallen out in some way
which meant that the TZ30 couldn't sort it's sequence of operations out. In
our case, the drive was just completely jammed (no reboot/powerdown would
fix it).  

In the end, I pulled the top of the drive to get to the guts of it, 
reconnected the leader and it all went back to normal.

