In article <CtvEnA.6Gw@serval.net.wsu.edu>, 
    			jpeterse@che.wsu.edu (James N. Petersen) writes:

> We are having problems getting the latest version of eXcursion
> to work with VMS hosts via tcp/ip transports.  In particular,
> it seems that we cannot start sessions on the VMS machines, however
> we can on ultrix machines and on OSF machines without any problems.
> We can log onto the VMS machine, set the display, and start
> decw$session on the remote pc, and then can start applications
> from the decw$session window.  We cannot start decw$terminal by
> from the VMS machine and have it display on the remote pc.
> 
> We have submitted the problem to DEC, but no solution yet.  I am
> wondering if others have seen this problem, and if anyone has 
> any ideas of how to solve it.

        As a "make sure  it's  plugged  in"  first  step, check that the
    TCP/IP  transport is enabled for DECwindows on the VMS system.  Look
    in  SYS$MANAGER:DECW$PRIVATE_SERVER_SETUP.COM  (which  is  a   site-
    specific  tailoring of the associated .TEMPLATE file), and make sure
    the line:

        $ decw$server_transports == "DECNET,LOCAL,LAT,TCPIP"

    includes "TCPIP", and is not commented out.  Without TCP/IP enabled
    _for_ DECwindows, you won't be able to display applications to _any_
    server that is accessible only by TCP/IP.

        -Ken
