dougcc@brt.deakin.edu.au (Douglas Miller) writes:
>
>In design and performance, FNEWS is by far the best of about 5 news
>readers for VMS that I have tried.

I've been working with FNEWS fro some time and agree that it's blazingly fast,
but it has a number of oddities that can make it awkward to get running
reliably at first.

The last version I have seen also has a number of bugs in it. I have sent the
author fixes to wuite a number of them, but I have never received any
indication that he has folded them into the regular distribution.

Unlike most news readers, FNEWS is not just a user code. It relies on a system
(cluster) based cache of indicies containing title and newsgroup information on
newsgroups that have been accessed recently and must run periodic batch jobs to
keep these up to date. This typically mean that it requires a system install,
so if you are a non-privileged user, you won't be able to do it yourself.

All that said, I like FNEWS and use it as my primary news reader, mostly
because it is so fast.

