In article <31jck4$98k@FERRARI.NMC.ED.RAY.COM>, heiser@ed.ray.com (Bill Heiser) writes:
> On a DS5000 running Ultrix 4.2, is it safe to assume that a write-protected
> floppy disk in an RX-23 drive is Really write protected?  What I mean is
> "is the write-protect tab an indicator to the SOFTWARE" or is it truly
> a HARDWARE write-protection that CAN'T be over-ridden by the kernel?

If you're talking a 5000/2xx or a 5000/1xx, where the floppy's out on the
SCSI bus, it's an indication to the microprocessor on the SCSI floppy
controller; if the disk is write protected, the microprocessor will refuse
to write the floppy, no matter what the kernel tells it.

On the 5000/xx, where the floppy's on the motherboard, I haven't the foggiest.
